  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">100 % reports on the application of ratified Conventions submitted  by the Government of Indonesia and received in a timely manner by the ILO in 2020.  ILO provided technical guidance to clarify and ensure that the Government replies to the Supervisory Body&apos;s comments in the report. In 2020 for example, ILO encouraged the Government to send the report in timely and consultative manners despite only additional information needed to the 2019 reports and difficulty for organizing consultation with the social partners due to pandemic. The same approach of providing assistance to Government continued in 2021</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3.1. Percentage of reports on the application of ratified Conventions due by 1 September received in a timely manner that include replies to comments of the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
